ign=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$9$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"85\" width=\"60\">\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\boxed{\\text{0}}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nWe get $\\boxed{\\text{0}}$, so the division is done.\n\nThe quotient is the sum of the numbers on top of the boxes:\n\n$$\n50+30+5=85\n$$\n\nTherefore, each roll has $85\\,\\text{m}$ of fabric."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138329 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91fb4b28-4839-575a-94ad-e9733650d129" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Number by Ten"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6c8494f-b16a-5986-b04a-52437f83ffe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6c8494f-b16a-5986-b04a-52437f83ffe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445304} :answer-field/id #uuid "70597078-f4fd-5d33-b6e1-7b9efe3946fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445311}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "95a90288-1c66-51f3-8327-26709f04b266" :question/math-academy-id "q-166770" :question/problem "Monica bought $10\\,\\text{m}$ of cotton fabric and paid $$39.50.$ What is the price per meter of cotton fabric?\n\nExpressed as a **decimal number**, a meter of cotton fabric costs $ \n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The meter of cotton fabric costs $$(39.50÷10).$\n\nTo perform this division, all we need to do is move the decimal point one place to the left:\n\n$$\n39.50\\to 3.950=3.95\n$$\n\nTherefore, $39.50÷10=3.95.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445318 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064158 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d20bb661-d55b-5db1-a353-a6d088ed3f86" :knowledge-point/title "Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f42abcde-18da-58ae-82a1-21e9df0d6cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.43" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f42abcde-18da-58ae-82a1-21e9df0d6cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.43" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445306} :answer-field/id #uuid "473457c1-8e08-59c3-a98c-5f53900769e9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7df42d1b-4cec-5d78-8cd7-de98b310c091" :question/math-academy-id "q-166771" :question/problem "A meter of drill fabric costs $$3.48.$ If Anna bought one meter of cotton fabric and one meter of drill fabric, in total, she paid $$${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "In part 2, we found that one meter of cotton fabric costs $$3.95.$\n\nTo find the total cost, we need to calculate the value of $3.95+3.48.$\n\nFirst, we line up the decimal points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we proceed by adding the two numbers just as we would with whole numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n3.95+3.48=7.43.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total cost is $$7.43.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445316 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138340 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c331171-b536-55c6-92d9-6d22b9200a05" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Decimal by a Whole Number: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bb55442-b865-5577-b007-562ca745e516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52.20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bb55442-b865-5577-b007-562ca745e516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52.20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445301} :answer-field/id #uuid "702a575b-0f02-5112-9f67-849c6e333818" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "43e5a6a2-9436-51e4-a444-4829716961e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-166772" :question/problem "Carmen, an experienced seamstress, bought $15\\,\\text{m}$ of drill fabric. The total she paid, expressed as a **decimal number**, was $$${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find out the amount of money that Carmen must pay, we need to multiply $15$ by $3.48.$\n\nWe proceed by multiplying the two numbers just as we would with whole numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{2}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{4}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,.4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now count the total number of decimal places in the two factors.\n\nThere are $2$ decimal places in $3.48.$ \nTherefore, the product will also have $2$ decimal places.\n\nSo, we take our value of $5220$ and add a decimal point to make a number with $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\n52\\,\\overset{↓}{.}\\,\\,\\,{{20}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ digits}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Carmen must pay $$3.48\\times 15=$52.20.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445322 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142811 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0261453-d071-5dbf-8d63-39c77ab39c72" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Result as a Mixed Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80e8c721-00c6-52fa-9c87-aa630d796ce8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80e8c721-00c6-52fa-9c87-aa630d796ce8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445302} :answer-field/id #uuid "10ea190f-2b81-55d5-aae9-2f2c1fbbbaf2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e72e7ec5-9f77-5705-95ed-eadc3761bae8" :question/math-academy-id "q-166773" :question/problem "Carmen cuts a piece of drill fabric with a length of $2\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{m}$ to make a tablecloth. If the fabric has a width of $1\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{m},$ what will be the area of the tablecloth? Express your answer as a **mixed number** in simplest form.\n\nThe tablecloth will have an area of\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The tablecloth will have an area of $(2\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\times 1\\,\\frac{1}{2}){\\text{m}}^{2}.$\n\nFirst, we write $2\\,\\frac{1}{4}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{(2\\times 4)+1}{4}=\\frac{9}{4}\n$$\n\nWe also write $1\\,\\frac{1}{2}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{(1\\times 2)+1}{2}=\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{4}\\times \\frac{3}{2}=\\frac{9\\times 3}{4\\times 2}=\\frac{27}{8}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{27}{8}=3\\,\\text{R}3=3\\,\\frac{3}{8}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445321 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138377 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "05636e74-7815-5a97-92a0-e29c2804d419" :knowledge-point/title "Adding Fractions Using the Least Common Multiple"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a68bafd-e384-5f9b-83b4-e06cb2184c8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{89}{42}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a68bafd-e384-5f9b-83b4-e06cb2184c8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{89}{42}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445303} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8ed4fae-048d-5f03-b27c-895a7582dfc5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445313}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d13eae43-32e2-575a-85c2-71abf6bbd783" :question/math-academy-id "q-166774" :question/problem "Carmen cuts two pieces of drill fabric with lengths of $\\frac{5}{6}\\,\\text{m}$ and $\\frac{9}{7}\\,\\text{m}.$ The sum of the lengths of the two pieces of fabric is{{field-1}}$\\text{m}.$" :question/worked-solution "The sum of the lengths of the two pieces of fabric is $(\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{9}{7})\\text{m}.$\n\nTo add two fractions with unlike denominators, we need to express each fraction as an equivalent fraction with a common denominator.\n\nLet's look at the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{9}{7}\n$$\n\nThe least common denominator of $6$ and $7$ is $42.$\n\nTo put $\\frac{5}{6}$ over a denominator of $42,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $7:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{5\\times 7}{6\\times 7}=\\frac{35}{42}\n$$\n\nTo put $\\frac{9}{7}$ over a denominator of $42,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{7}=\\frac{9\\times 6}{7\\times 6}=\\frac{54}{42}\n$$\n\nWe can now add the fractions. We keep the denominator the same, and we add the numerators.\n\n$$\n\\frac{35}{42}+\\frac{54}{42}=\\frac{89}{42}\n$$\n\nExpressing this fraction as a mixed number, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{89}{42}=2\\,\\frac{5}{42}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the lengths of the two pieces of fabric is $2\\,\\frac{5}{42}\\,\\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445319 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138577 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c87e441-a534-5f6b-82e7-34e2ef8b9639" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting Two Mixed Numbers Using the Least Common Denominator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5adf5daf-1367-5822-9ec3-09c2b43dc829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\frac{1}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5adf5daf-1367-5822-9ec3-09c2b43dc829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\frac{1}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445300} :answer-field/id #uuid "16254907-0b98-5e04-a2ea-99f6a0c12803" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86788b5f-c043-547d-a152-64c87d27af72" :question/math-academy-id "q-166775" :question/problem "Carmen has a piece of fabric with a length of $5\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{m}.$ She accidentally spills coffee on this piece, so she decides to cut out and discard $1\\,\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{m}$ of fabric. How long is the remaining piece of fabric? Express your answer as a **mixed number** in simplest form.\n\nThe remaining piece of fabric has a length of\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}.$" :question/worked-solution "The new piece of fabric has a length of $(5\\,\\frac{1}{4}-1\\,\\frac{1}{5})\\text{m}$ long.\n\nTo subtract two mixed numbers, we subtract whole numbers from whole numbers and fractions from fractions.\n\nSubtracting the whole numbers, we get $5-1=4.$ \n\nNow we subtract the fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nLet's look at the denominators. The least common denominator of $4$ and $5$ is $20.$\n\nTo put $\\frac{1}{4}$ over a denominator of $20,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1\\times 5}{4\\times 5}=\\frac{5}{20}\n$$\n\nTo put $\\frac{1}{5}$ over a denominator of $20,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{1\\times 4}{5\\times 4}=\\frac{4}{20}\n$$\n\nWe can now subtract the fractions. We keep the denominator the same, and we subtract the numerators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{5}{20}-\\frac{4}{20}=\\frac{1}{20}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n5\\,\\frac{1}{4}-1\\,\\frac{1}{5}=4\\,\\frac{1}{20}.\n$$"}]}
